course: dictionary
lesson: 14282
title: Compass words: northwards
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Northwards means towards the north. It tells you which way something is moving. «The hikers set off northwards at dawn.» Swap in your meaning: "The hikers set off towards the north at dawn" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Northwards is an adverb, so it often comes after a movement word such as «head» or «move». «The storm began to move northwards across the sea.» Northward, without the s, is also used, as in «a northward route» for a path that goes towards the north.
explain: Northwards belongs to a family of compass words: southwards, eastwards and westwards. Learn them as a set, and you can read directions on any map or in any travel story.
fact: Northwards means towards the north.
fact: The other compass directions work the same way: southwards, eastwards and westwards.
fact: Birds fly northwards in spring in the Northern Hemisphere.
fact: On a map, north is usually at the top.
fact: Common phrases in geography include «head northwards» and «move northwards».
exercise: «The geese flew northwards over the lake in spring.» Which way did the geese fly? | Towards the east | Round in circles | *Towards the north | Towards the south
exercise: On a map, where is north usually shown? | In the middle | On the left side | *At the top | At the bottom
exercise: Which compass word means towards the south? | *Southwards | Northern | Upwards | Eastwards
test: «The walkers will head northwards after lunch.» What does northwards mean? | *Towards the north | Backwards | Very quickly | Towards the sea
test: Which compass word means towards the west? | Northwards | Southern | *Westwards | Eastwards
exam: «The storm moved northwards, and the ferry sailed southwards to stay safe.» Which way did the ferry sail? | Towards the east | *Towards the south | Towards the north | Towards the west
